; Bitmap copy chain going back (last 10 LDD), then the next pixel row
;
; The end of the chain of #R$9685, the plain copy of the first cell's byte, then HL and DE go to the next pixel row
; (the next page of the redraw buffers, 256 bytes further in the screen). It falls into the JR at #R$96C7, which enters
; the chain of LDI instructions at #R$96C9 to copy the next pixel row from the first cell to the last.
; .
; Hardware: writes the screen bitmap.
;
; HL Redraw buffer address of the first cell
; DE Screen bitmap address of the first cell
; O:HL Page + 1 of the first cell
; O:DE Screen address + $0100: pixel row + 1 of the first cell
@label=CopyBitmapBack_Tail
c$96AF LDD           ;
 $96B1 LDD           ;
 $96B3 LDD           ;
 $96B5 LDD           ;
 $96B7 LDD           ;
 $96B9 LDD           ;
 $96BB LDD           ;
 $96BD LDD           ;
 $96BF LDD           ;
 $96C1 LDD           ;
 $96C3 LD A,(HL)     ;
 $96C4 LD (DE),A     ;
 $96C5 INC H         ;
 $96C6 INC D         ;
; Self-modified: the offset byte of this JR is written by #R$9615 (2 x (32 - run length)). It enters the chain of LDI
; instructions at #R$96C9 to copy one pixel row of the run from its first cell to its last.
@label=SmcBitmapForwardJump
*$96C7 JR $96C7      ; enter the LDI chain; the offset byte (+1) is patched
